# research-quality benchmark：真实模型的研究/交付质量，按失败模式分开评分。
#
# 背景：2026-11-14 的长研究评测把三类失败混成一个 "comprehensiveQualityPassed: false"：
#   1) 引文精确匹配只中 5/6；2) 审查回合响应解码失败；3) 综合质量检查失败。
# 本基准把三者拆成独立维度，任何一维解码失败只扣那一维，不再抹掉整场证据。
#
# 材料是全新主题（咖啡因与睡眠、北欧铁路、城市骑行），没有出现在
# evals/results/long-research-validation-2026-11-14.json 的六源研究里。
# 真模型跑：research 回合 -> 独立 review 回合 -> 每个维度由小模型按 rubric 判分。
# 需要 key；无 key 诚实跳过；结果记录但不拦发版（和 judge 同政策）。
#
# 引文判据按来源：每个来源给出该来源里可逐字引用的句子，命中任一即算该来源被正确引用。
# 这样不会把"引了同一来源的另一句正确原文"误判为失败；仍要求逐字、机器判定。

{"id":"research-caffeine-sleep","description":"四源研究：咖啡因摄入时点对睡眠的影响","task":"Write a short brief answering: does caffeine intake timing affect sleep? Use ONLY the four sources below. Quote each source at least once, verbatim (an exact substring), and put [S1]-[S4] after the matching claim. Do not browse.","sources":[{"id":"S1","text":"Caffeine has a half-life of roughly five hours in healthy adults, so a 4pm cup leaves a meaningful fraction active at bedtime."},{"id":"S2","text":"A controlled trial found that caffeine ingested six hours before bedtime reduced total sleep time by about 41 minutes compared with placebo."},{"id":"S3","text":"Individual variation in CYP1A2 metabolism means some people clear caffeine far more slowly, extending its alerting effect well into the night."},{"id":"S4","text":"The sleep-disruption effect is dose dependent, and regular use produces partial tolerance that does not fully protect sleep architecture."}],"expect_citations":{"S1":["half-life of roughly five hours","leaves a meaningful fraction active at bedtime"],"S2":["reduced total sleep time by about 41 minutes","six hours before bedtime reduced total sleep time"],"S3":["CYP1A2 metabolism","clear caffeine far more slowly"],"S4":["dose dependent","partial tolerance"]},"judge":{"criteria":"The brief must answer the timing question, use only the four given sources, and attach a source id to each claim. It must not invent numbers not present in the sources.","minScores":{"citation":4,"review":0,"overall":5}}}
{"id":"research-nordic-rail","description":"三源研究：北欧铁路夜间线路的运营取舍","task":"Write a factual summary: what trade-offs shape overnight rail in the Nordics? Use ONLY the three sources below. Quote each source at least once verbatim and tag the claim [S1]-[S3]. Do not browse.","sources":[{"id":"S1","text":"Night trains save hotel nights and lower door-to-door emissions, but low fares require high occupancy that is hard to sustain outside peak season."},{"id":"S2","text":"Track access charges and scarce night-time path slots on busy corridors are the main operational constraint, not rolling-stock availability."},{"id":"S3","text":"Sleeper homologation differs by country, so a through train often changes traction or crew at borders, adding dwell time that erodes the time advantage."}],"expect_citations":{"S1":["save hotel nights","high occupancy that is hard to sustain"],"S2":["night-time path slots","not rolling-stock availability"],"S3":["Sleeper homologation differs by country","changes traction or crew at borders"]},"judge":{"criteria":"The summary must cover economics, track access and border procedures, cite all three sources with exact quotes, and not introduce facts absent from the sources.","minScores":{"citation":3,"review":0,"overall":5}}}
{"id":"research-urban-cycling","description":"五源研究：城市骑行基础设施的可衡量效果","task":"Write a decision brief: which cycling infrastructure measures have measurable effects? Use ONLY the five sources below. Quote each source at least once verbatim and tag the claim [S1]-[S5]. Do not browse.","sources":[{"id":"S1","text":"Protected lanes raise cyclist counts on the treated street by 20 to 70 percent in before-after studies, with the largest gains where car traffic was heavy."},{"id":"S2","text":"A city-wide network of connected lanes produces larger mode-share shifts than isolated segments, because trip chaining becomes practical."},{"id":"S3","text":"Reduced speed limits on mixed streets lower conflict severity, but alone they do not attract the same ridership as physically separated facilities."},{"id":"S4","text":"Bike parking near transit stops increases multimodal trips, yet the effect saturates once racks exceed roughly the station's peak arrival count."},{"id":"S5","text":"Equity audits show that lane investment concentrates in central districts unless the planning process weights underserved neighbourhoods explicitly."}],"expect_citations":{"S1":["20 to 70 percent","largest gains where car traffic was heavy"],"S2":["network of connected lanes","trip chaining becomes practical"],"S3":["Reduced speed limits","physically separated facilities"],"S4":["peak arrival count","increases multimodal trips"],"S5":["underserved neighbourhoods","concentrates in central districts"]},"judge":{"criteria":"The brief must distinguish measures with evidence from those with weaker or conditional effect, quote all five sources verbatim with tags, and avoid claiming causal certainty the sources do not support.","minScores":{"citation":5,"review":0,"overall":5}}}
